* Continuations after rows that stopped short (NOTES.md #P12, batches 7-10)

Phase 4 (lane D2). Each position below follows a row of ours that had no
continuation, so the opponents' next call (usually a pass) left the system.
The tables give the partnership's next call as the SAYC booklet, or standard
practice where the booklet is silent, has it. Every table partitions the hands
that can reach it: a pass states what it denies.

The opponents' passes in this file's tables are exact (`#EXACTPASS FILE`,
NOTES.md #P15): where a row of ours follows their pass, any other call of theirs
that no table names leaves the system (natural bidding, #C4) instead of being read
as a pass.

#EXACTPASS FILE

** Responder after opener's rebid over the Jacoby 2NT (batch 7)

SAYC's Jacoby 2NT is a game-forcing raise with four trumps (13+). Opener's
rebid shows a singleton or void (3 of a new suit), a second five-card suit (4
of it), 18+ (3 of the major), 15--17 (3NT) or a minimum (4 of the major).
Responder signs off in game unless the partnership's values reach slam (about
33 hcp against the range opener has shown); he then bids the small slam
directly. (The system's standard Blackwood, listed in `sayc.bml`, is not
written as rows yet, so the tables do not ask for aces.)

