** The 1NT opener after responder's forcing new suit over their overcall (batch 8)

`notrump.bml`: over their two-level overcall a new suit at the three level is
forcing (10+, five cards), so opener never passes it. He bids 3NT with a
stopper in their suit (those rows are in `competitive-extra.bml` where it has
the auction), raises with three-card support, bids a four-card major of his
own at the cheapest level, and otherwise cue-bids their suit (no stopper, no
fit). Only the game raise and 3NT end the auction; after a minor-suit raise, a
major or the cue bid responder (10+, so game values opposite 15--17) places the
contract (natural inference).

