** Passes that end a limited auction (batch 9)

When partner's last call is non-forcing and limited, the hand that has nothing
to add passes. Each pass below is bounded by the strength the earlier bidding
already shows and by the ranges of its invitational siblings. (Where an earlier
file already ends the row with `#STOP` -- 1M-1NT, 1M-2M, 1M-3M, 1M-1NT-2NT,
1M-1NT-2m, 1!s-1NT-2!h and 1m-1M-2M -- the system's stop pass is the pass and
is not repeated here.)

After opener's 2NT rebid (18--19) and responder's 3NT there is no slam to
look for.

1M-(P)-1N-(P)-2N-(P)-3N-(P)-
P = {prio:0} 18--19 hcp
  #STOP

Opener's rebid of a six-card major over 1NT is 12--15: responder passes.

