** Opener passes partner's game sign-off (batch 10)

A game bid that partner chooses from a limited range is to play. Opener
passes it without slam values: 12--15 opposite partner's game range leaves no
slam. Stronger hands are not written; they are the partnership's judgment.

After responder's 3NT (13--15 balanced) over opener's one-level new suit. That
rebid is 12--18 and unbalanced, so only its minimum passes here; 16--18 has
slam interest opposite 13--15 and gets no row.

